release: 2026.6.13
resolution: Work completed and released in 2026.6.13. Release attribution set explicitly so pm-changelog --respect-item-release files the entry under 2026.6.13 instead of the current release notes.
expected_result: "A closed item whose changelog entry appears under the 2026.6.13 heading it actually shipped in, leaving the current release notes untouched."
actual_result: "Item remained in_progress with no activity after its work shipped, so the delivery was absent from the changelog while still counting as open work in every fleet audit."
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-06-07T07:55:26.408Z",codex-5.3-full-cycle,"pm-web release:check passed after dependency alignment and generated frontend JS cleanup from git-tracked sources."
  "2026-06-07T08:00:45.580Z",codex-5.3-full-cycle,"Security gate: high-confidence token/key regex scan over tracked files and git history found no actionable secrets. Binary-history false positives were traced to embedded wasm base64 blobs, not credentials."
  "2026-06-12T11:53:16.482Z",codex-audit,"2026-06-12 package/release audit: release workflow contains unresolved merge-conflict markers and is invalid YAML. package.json is private:true but release.yml includes npm publish, so publish intent is contradictory. TypeScript-only compliance gap: public/src has tracked generated .js and .js.map alongside .ts sources. Dev/lock dependencies are staged to latest @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.6.12 and pm-changelog 2026.6.10. Files to review: .github/workflows/release.yml, package.json, package-lock.json, .gitignore, public/src/**/*.js, public/src/**/*.js.map."
files[4]{path,scope,note}:
  .gitignore,project,Ignore generated frontend JS/JS.map artifacts to keep TS sources canonical
  extensions/pm-graph/package.json,project,Updated embedded extension dependency baseline
  package.json,project,Updated pm CLI/changelog devDependencies to latest
  public/src/app.ts,project,Frontend TypeScript source-of-truth entrypoint
tests[1]{command,path,scope,timeout_seconds}:
  "npm run release:check",.,project,3600
close_reason: "Retired as shipped: the full-cycle hardening wave for pm-web was completed and released in 2026.6.13, but the item was never closed and sat in progress ever since, inflating every fleet audit."
body: Track pm-web TS/readiness hardening evidence.
